    {
        "content": "<p>rvolosatovs opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14627\">PR #14627</a> from <code>rvolosatovs:fix/copy-gc-roots</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>Table::copy</code> copies each element by reading it with <code>Table::get</code> and writing it with <code>Table::set</code>. For GC reference tables, <code>Table::get</code> creates a LIFO <code>Rooted</code> in the caller's current root scope. Nothing in <code>Table::copy</code> released those roots, so when it was called on a plain <code>&amp;mut Store</code> rather than inside a <code>RootScope</code>, every copied object stayed rooted until the store was dropped. Repeated copies grew the root set and kept the GC heap from shrinking across collections.</p>\n<p>Enter a GC LIFO scope around each element's get/set pair and exit it afterwards, so the temporary root is released before the next element is copied.</p>\n</blockquote>",
